WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.282
The headline evidence is how wildly performance
swings with the benchmark.

00:00:04.362 --> 00:00:08.643
One facial expression model, built on AlexNet,

00:00:08.723 --> 00:00:13.005
ranges from just 48.6 percent accuracy on SFEW to
94.8 percent on MultiPie,

00:00:13.085 --> 00:00:17.367
against a random baseline of 14.2 percent,

00:00:17.447 --> 00:00:21.728
so which benchmark you pick determines the story you tell.

00:00:21.808 --> 00:00:26.090
The pattern generalizes: when researchers
faithfully recreated the ImageNet and CIFAR-10 test sets,

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:30.452
state-of-the-art accuracy fell by three to fifteen
percent.

00:00:30.532 --> 00:00:34.813
And a leading DFDC deepfake detector assigned only
two and eight percent likelihood to

00:00:34.893 --> 00:00:39.175
genuine deepfakes of Kim Jong-un and Vladimir Putin,

00:00:39.255 --> 00:00:43.537
precisely the high-context videos that matter in
the real world.

00:00:43.617 --> 00:00:47.898
In dermatology,

00:00:47.978 --> 00:00:52.260
benchmarks that barely include dark skin let
systematic errors hide in plain sight.
